    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean, \"balanced\" sounds good on paper, but in a public meeting, parents aren't looking for a middle ground. they want to know what works. if you had to choose, wouldn't focusing on systemic injustices actually be more effective for teaching kids how to think critically about the world instead of just memorizing a \"feel good\" version of history?",
